{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/707485-compact-brothers-and-sisters-of-escape","id":707485,"title":"(Compact) Brothers and Sisters of Escape","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-18T15:12:45-07:00","id":707485,"title":"(Compact) Brothers and Sisters of Escape","content":"(And this is what happens when you play Prison Architect until 4 in the morning.)<br /> <br /> At a supermax in the United States, fourteen inmates have disappeared, five guards are dead, and the Warden's entrails are all over his office. Of the inmates, one of them was imprisoned for a murder with a knife, despite marks at the scene suggesting claws. Those who escaped will disappear without a trace, who knows where by the time the investigation finally gives up. <br /> <br /> Last week,over 500 inmates escaped from an overcrowded Californian prison, somehow tunneling through solid concrete. This week, two judges, and five cops are dead, with, &quot;LIAR,&quot; painted all over their homes. Further investigation suggests the original prosecution was built on faulty evidence, and that the judges received bribes for extending sentences as much as possible. Attempts to cover this up fail, from a journalist given a tip by an unknown caller. The escapees will never be found, although glimpses seem to be caught of them helping others escape over the course of the years. <br /> <br /> A city trembles when the mayor is brutally murdered by escaped convicts. The murder seems to be in response to him banning family visitation for the local prison. Terror spreads even more when it is learned all the convicts were serial killers, and that they will soon be starting a brand new murder spree. Worst of all, the only ones who can stop them are still in jail, as only they know where the killers are. Their price is the return of family visitation, and oddly, nothing else. <br /> <br /> Political dissidents will escape prison in Iran, and be given to the United States. In return for this arrangement, a corruption investigation shall begin in the state of Kentucky, and will end with dozens of cops arrested for tampering with evidence in a way to allow a variety of arrests. The dissidents will be unable to explain how they actually got out, describing it as, &quot;magic.&quot; And the evidence tampering arose from police desperate to get someone for crimes that the city wouldn't accept no suspect turning up for. <br /> <br /> <br /> They aren't a traditional hunter organization, although they have killed quite a few monsters in their time. Their only goal is to get those wrongfully imprisoned out of jail, although they do dish out punishment to those who put them there in the first place. However, more often than one might think, entities like Werewolves, or even Witches, can find themselves in jail. And the organization itself has strange tricks of its own. <br /> <br /> But, there's a much bigger reason they are seen as hunters. Countless supernatural crimes are covered up by using a mortal to take the blame instead. More than that, many victims of the supernatural end up imprisoned because of the nature of what happened to them, and those around them. The response to both of these is to seek out, and brutally punish those who would use imprisonment as a way to cover up their crimes, or the crimes of others. So the Brothers and Sisters of Escape are known as Hunters, despite that hunting the supernatural is far from their primary goal. <br /> <br /> Complicating matters is that the Brothers and Sisters of Escape are more than willing to break people out of jail if, in return, others are helped to escape, and those responsible for the imprisonment are punished. Even serial killers have escaped through this arrangement, although they frequently find themselves dead if they abuse the privilege of escape too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T23:39:37-07:00","id":734004,"title":"","content":"<b>History</b><br /> <br /> The Brothers and Sisters of Escape have existed as early as Colonial America, if their founding myth is to be believed. A woman falsely accused of being a Witch, rather than suffer death, escaped prison through the help of a man with strange tricks, but whom never sought to harm anyone. Once they escaped, they went on to hunt down and kill the actual monster, disguised as the town's priest. However, knowing the town would never believe their side of the story, they ran into the wilderness, where they managed a successful life of agriculture. <br /> <br /> Their children, it is said, would go on to found an organization devoted to breaking out those unjustly imprisoned. Whether one believes this myth isn't quite as important as what it represents to the organization, that some supernatural entities can be trusted, while others will use human prejudice and the human legal system to cover up their own crimes. Hence, the need to break those blamed falsely out of prison, and punish those who would use them for their own gains. <br /> <br /> The first known presence of the organization was in the 19th century, where they broke people out of prison in the Eastern United States, and began hunting down the monsters who utilized the legal system to their advantage. This frequently meant attacking people in power, however the aid of supernatural entities, and the ability to get out of jail if they ended up in it, made this a far easier task. <br /> <br /> However, it was in the 20th century that two very important components of the organization would be born. The first was utilizing the power of political asylum to buy bargaining power with the state, and facilitate political change to help their cause. The second was a larger focus on trying to change the conditions of the prison system through political reform, however intractable that would be in the United States. Both changes arose out of the organization growing in scale, and gaining far more members, but also running into that the problem they sought to deal with was because of systematic flaws in legal systems that let them be far too exploitable by supernatural entities. <br /> <br /> All of this lead to the Compact as it is today. The sheer number of people broken out of prison per year has grown to the thousands, and they've spread to every major continent on the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}